      "params": {
        "text": "## Try it\nFlip **A** and **B**. Every gate on the left sees\nexactly the same two inputs, so the six lamps are\ntheir truth tables, read one row at a time.",
        "format": "markdown",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "align": "left",
        "color": "default",
        "background": "none",
        "width": 30,
        "height": 9
      }
    },
    "n_note_bubbles": {
      "id": "n_note_bubbles",
      "type": "deco.text",
      "position": {
        "x": 610,
        "y": 230
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "### About those bubbles\nThe lower three gates are the upper three with a\nbubble on the output, and a bubble means *invert*.\n**NAND**, **NOR** and **XNOR** always answer the\nopposite way to the gate above them.\n\nSet **A** and **B** the same and you can watch it:\nevery lamp on the left goes dark exactly when its\npartner on the right lights up.",
        "format": "markdown",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "align": "left",
        "color": "default",
        "background": "none",
        "width": 30,
        "height": 15
      }
    },
